<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Representative Prompt Examples by Task Family</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This appendix provides representative prompt examples for the major task
families in our taxonomy. The examples are abstracted from recurring
input–output needs in the surveyed systems. They are not verbatim prompts from
any single paper, and they are not intended to define a separate taxonomy of
prompt types.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Forecasting and Reasoning</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para"><code id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨System:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨You are a time-series analysis agent.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Use temporal evidence, retrieved context,<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨and tool outputs to produce a grounded<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨forecast, answer, or classification. Do<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨not rely on unsupported patterns.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨User:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Task:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Forecast the target horizon, or answer<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  the temporal reasoning or classification<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  question.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.14" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.15" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Inputs:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.16" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Historical observations:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.17" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;series or summarized windows&gt;<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.18" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Target horizon or question:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.19" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;forecast horizon / question&gt;<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.20" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Retrieved analogs or external context:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.21" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;optional&gt;<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.22" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Candidate hypotheses or exemplars:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.23" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;optional&gt;<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.24" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Tool outputs:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.25" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;trend, seasonality, anomaly,<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.26" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   correlation, model scores&gt;<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.27" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.28" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Instructions:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.29" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨1. Identify trend, seasonality, local<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.30" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   changes, and unusual events.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.31" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨2. Select evidence relevant to the<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.32" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   horizon or question.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.33" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨3. Compare candidate hypotheses or<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.34" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   retrieved exemplars when provided.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.35" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨4. Use tool outputs for quantitative<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.36" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   claims.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.37" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨5. Produce the forecast, answer, or label<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.38" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   with a concise rationale.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.39" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨6. State uncertainty and failure modes.<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.40" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.41" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Output JSON:<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.42" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨{<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.43" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "evidence_summary": "…",<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.44" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "reasoning": "…",<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.45" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "prediction_answer_or_label": "…",<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.46" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "confidence": "…",<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.47" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "limitations": "…"<span id="A2.SS1.p1.1.48" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨}<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="38.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 38.29" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,38.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000099;" fill="#000099" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.35 L 0 33.94 C 0 36.34 1.95 38.29 4.35 38.29 L 648.8 38.29 C 651.2 38.29 653.15 36.34 653.15 33.94 L 653.15 4.35 C 653.15 1.95 651.2 0 648.8 0 L 4.35 0 C 1.95 0 0 1.95 0 4.35 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0F9FF;" fill="#F0F9FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 4.35 L 0.42 33.94 C 0.42 36.11 2.18 37.87 4.35 37.87 L 648.8 37.87 C 650.97 37.87 652.73 36.11 652.73 33.94 L 652.73 4.35 C 652.73 2.18 650.97 0.42 648.8 0.42 L 4.35 0.42 C 2.18 0.42 0.42 2.18 0.42 4.35 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.29 15.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="636.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A2.SS1.p1.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>This example reflects common input–output needs in forecasting and reasoning
agents such as TimeSeriesScientist <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2025)</a></cite>,
TimeXL <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jiang et al. (2025)</a></cite>, TS-Agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025)</a></cite>, and
TS-Reasoner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. (2024b)</a></cite>.

<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Augmentation and Synthesis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para"><code id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨System:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨You are assisting time-series data<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨construction. Augment a target series or<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨synthesize a controlled series only when<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨the requested temporal semantics and<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨domain constraints can be preserved.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨User:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.10" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Task:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.11" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Create an augmented example, synthetic<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.12" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  series, or textual annotation.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.13" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.14" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Inputs:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.15" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Construction mode:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.16" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;target augmentation | text-guided<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.17" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   synthesis | domain-attribute synthesis&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.18" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Seed series or source examples:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.19" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;values / windows / examples&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.20" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Desired label, scenario, or query:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.21" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;class, event, scenario, or description&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.22" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Required temporal properties:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.23" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;trend, periodicity, volatility, extrema&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.24" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Domain constraints:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.25" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;valid ranges, correlations,<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.26" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   physical rules&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.27" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Validation criteria:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.28" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;downstream check or consistency rule&gt;<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.29" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.30" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Instructions:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.31" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨1. Preserve task-relevant temporal<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.32" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   semantics when augmenting a target<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.33" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   series.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.34" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨2. Align control text or domain attributes<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.35" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   with the generated series when<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.36" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   synthesizing new data.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.37" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨3. Apply only transformations consistent<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.38" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   with the label or scenario.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.39" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨4. Avoid changing causal, seasonal, or<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.40" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   domain-critical structure.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.41" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨5. Explain which properties are preserved<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.42" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   or intentionally changed.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.43" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨6. Return a compact structured result for<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.44" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   downstream validation.<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.45" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.46" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Output JSON:<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.47" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨{<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.48" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "construction_mode": "…",<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.49" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "constructed_item": "…",<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.50" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "control_attributes": "…",<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.51" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨¯  "preserved_properties": "…",<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.52" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "changed_properties": "…",<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.53" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "validation_notes": "…"<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.54" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨}<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS2.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="38.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 38.29" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,38.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#007300;" fill="#007300" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.35 L 0 33.94 C 0 36.34 1.95 38.29 4.35 38.29 L 648.8 38.29 C 651.2 38.29 653.15 36.34 653.15 33.94 L 653.15 4.35 C 653.15 1.95 651.2 0 648.8 0 L 4.35 0 C 1.95 0 0 1.95 0 4.35 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#ECFDF5;" fill="#ECFDF5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 4.35 L 0.42 33.94 C 0.42 36.11 2.18 37.87 4.35 37.87 L 648.8 37.87 C 650.97 37.87 652.73 36.11 652.73 33.94 L 652.73 4.35 C 652.73 2.18 650.97 0.42 648.8 0.42 L 4.35 0.42 C 2.18 0.42 0.42 2.18 0.42 4.35 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.29 15.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="636.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A2.SS2.p1.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>This example reflects common input–output needs in augmentation and synthesis
systems such as TESSA <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib45" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin et al. (2026)</a></cite>, MERIT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2025)</a></cite>,
BRIDGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2025)</a></cite>, and ChatTS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xie et al. (2025)</a></cite>.

<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Anomaly Detection and Diagnosis</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para"><code id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨System:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨You are a time-series monitoring agent.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Convert detector evidence, temporal<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨context, and auxiliary logs into a<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨supported alarm, point/window label, or<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨diagnostic explanation.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨User:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Task:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Decide whether the candidate window is<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  anomalous, or explain a fault.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Inputs:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Candidate window:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;time range and observed values&gt;<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Detector evidence:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.18" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;scores, thresholds, labels, residuals&gt;<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Temporal context:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.20" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;recent history, seasonality,<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.21" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   expected behavior&gt;<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.22" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Auxiliary context:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.23" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;logs, alerts, topology,<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.24" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   related variables&gt;<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.25" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Historical cases:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.26" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;optional retrieved examples&gt;<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.27" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.28" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Instructions:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.29" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨1. Compare the candidate window with<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.30" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   expected temporal behavior.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.31" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨2. Separate detector evidence from<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.32" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   contextual or textual evidence.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.33" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨3. Check whether context supports or<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.34" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   contradicts the detector evidence.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.35" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨4. Identify the most likely abnormal<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.36" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   interval or root cause.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.37" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨5. Avoid overriding the detector or<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.38" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   overclaiming when evidence is<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.39" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   weak or conflicting.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.40" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨6. Return a decision, supporting evidence,<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.41" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   and confidence.<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.42" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.43" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Output JSON:<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.44" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨{<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.45" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "decision": "normal | anomalous | uncertain",<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.46" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "abnormal_interval": "…",<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.47" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "supporting_evidence": "…",<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.48" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "root_cause_hypothesis": "…",<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.49" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "confidence": "…"<span id="A2.SS3.p1.1.50" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨}<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS3.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="38.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 38.29" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,38.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#B35900;" fill="#B35900" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.35 L 0 33.94 C 0 36.34 1.95 38.29 4.35 38.29 L 648.8 38.29 C 651.2 38.29 653.15 36.34 653.15 33.94 L 653.15 4.35 C 653.15 1.95 651.2 0 648.8 0 L 4.35 0 C 1.95 0 0 1.95 0 4.35 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFFBEB;" fill="#FFFBEB" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 4.35 L 0.42 33.94 C 0.42 36.11 2.18 37.87 4.35 37.87 L 648.8 37.87 C 650.97 37.87 652.73 36.11 652.73 33.94 L 652.73 4.35 C 652.73 2.18 650.97 0.42 648.8 0.42 L 4.35 0.42 C 2.18 0.42 0.42 2.18 0.42 4.35 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.29 15.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="636.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS3.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A2.SS3.p1.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>This example reflects common input–output needs in anomaly detection and
diagnosis systems such as SAGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib53" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kang et al. (2026)</a></cite>, ARGOS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gu et al. (2025)</a></cite>,
AgentFM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib65" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025a)</a></cite>, and LLM-TSFD <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025b)</a></cite>.

<section id="A2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.4 </span>Decision Support</h3>

<div id="A2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para"><code id="A2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_verbatim"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨System:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨You are a sequential decision-support<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨agent. Recommend only actions allowed by<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨the action space and supported by the<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨current temporal state, constraints, and<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.7" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨validation feedback.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨User:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Task:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Select the next trading, traffic-control,<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  or grid-control action.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.14" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Inputs:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.15" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Current state:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.16" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;market / intersection / grid state&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.17" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Recent history:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.18" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;prices, flows, loads, events,<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.19" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   or violations&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.20" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Historical experience:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.21" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;retrieved cases, lessons, or patterns&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.22" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- External evidence:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.23" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;news, indicators, forecasts,<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.24" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   alerts, optional&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.25" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Action space:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.26" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;allowed actions and parameter ranges&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.27" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Constraints:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.28" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;risk preference, safety limits,<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.29" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   policies, timing, feasibility&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.30" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨- Validation feedback:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.31" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  &lt;simulator, solver, or previous outcome&gt;<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.32" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.33" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Instructions:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.34" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨1. Summarize the state variables that<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.35" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   matter for the next action.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.36" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨2. Compare feasible actions under the<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.37" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   provided constraints.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.38" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨3. Use historical experience for<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.39" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   market-like settings when available.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.40" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨4. Use validation feedback to reject<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.41" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   unsafe or dominated actions.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.42" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨5. Recommend one action and explain the<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.43" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   expected effect.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.44" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨6. State the main risk and what should be<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.45" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨   monitored next.<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.46" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.47" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨Output JSON:<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.48" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨{<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.49" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "state_summary": "…",<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.50" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "recommended_action": "…",<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.51" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "justification": "…",<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.52" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "constraint_check": "…",<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.53" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨  "next_monitoring_target": "…"<span id="A2.SS4.p1.1.54" class="ltx_ERROR undefined">\iow_now:Ne</span>¨}<span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A2.SS4.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="38.29" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 653.15 38.29" width="653.15"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,38.29) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#530053;" fill="#530053" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 4.35 L 0 33.94 C 0 36.34 1.95 38.29 4.35 38.29 L 648.8 38.29 C 651.2 38.29 653.15 36.34 653.15 33.94 L 653.15 4.35 C 653.15 1.95 651.2 0 648.8 0 L 4.35 0 C 1.95 0 0 1.95 0 4.35 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F5F3FF;" fill="#F5F3FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.42 4.35 L 0.42 33.94 C 0.42 36.11 2.18 37.87 4.35 37.87 L 648.8 37.87 C 650.97 37.87 652.73 36.11 652.73 33.94 L 652.73 4.35 C 652.73 2.18 650.97 0.42 648.8 0.42 L 4.35 0.42 C 2.18 0.42 0.42 2.18 0.42 4.35 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 8.29 15.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:46.01em;--ltx-fo-height:0.75em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.25em;font-size:10pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="636.65"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A2.SS4.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-logical-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:46.01em;">
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.pic1.tab1" class="ltx_float ltx_lstlisting">
<span id="A2.SS4.p1.pic1.tab1.1" class="ltx_listing ltx_lstlisting ltx_listing">
</span>
</span></span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>This example reflects common input–output needs in decision-support systems
such as TradingAgents <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib70" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al. (2024)</a></cite>, FinCon <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yu et al. (2024)</a></cite>,
LLMLight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib116" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai et al. (2025)</a></cite>, and Grid-Agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025d)</a></cite>.


<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Typical Design Patterns</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A6.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ Decision and control metrics. ‣ Appendix F Evaluation Evidence and Metrics ‣ Appendix E Resources Summary ‣ Appendix D Failure Modes and Design Patterns ‣ Appendix C Typical Design Patterns ‣ B.4 Decision Support ‣ B.3 Anomaly Detection and Diagnosis ‣ B.2 Augmentation and Synthesis ‣ B.1 Forecasting and Reasoning ‣ Appendix B Representative Prompt Examples by Task Family ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> provides a supplementary visual summary of the typical design patterns discussed across different time-series tasks in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Taxonomy ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>. Each panel shows a common design pattern rather than the exact design of a specific system. Dashed boxes denote agent modules together with their tools, solid boxes group entities with similar roles, solid arrows show the main flow, dashed arrows indicate conditional or fallback paths, and background colors group panels from the same higher-level problem type.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Failure Modes and Design Patterns</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The task sections discuss these failure modes in context. Table <a href="#A4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ Appendix D Failure Modes and Design Patterns ‣ Appendix C Typical Design Patterns ‣ B.4 Decision Support ‣ B.3 Anomaly Detection and Diagnosis ‣ B.2 Augmentation and Synthesis ‣ B.1 Forecasting and Reasoning ‣ Appendix B Representative Prompt Examples by Task Family ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> brings them into one view and links each one to design choices reported in related work. The table is not a causal comparison; it is meant as a practical checklist for where a design choice helps and what should be inspected.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Summary of documented failure modes for time-series agent systems. Each failure mode is linked to related work, design choices, and implementation checks.</figcaption>
<div id="A4.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:330.9pt;vertical-align:-163.7pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-74.0pt,71.0pt) scale(0.699729459680059,0.699729459680059) ;">
<table id="A4.T2.2.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A4.T2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Failure mode</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A4.T2.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Where it appears</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A4.T2.2.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Related work</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A4.T2.2.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Design choice</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="A4.T2.2.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.T2.2.1.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Implementation check</span></span>
</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Error propagation across workflow stages</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Forecasting and reasoning pipelines that pass outputs through diagnosis, model selection, context analysis, prediction, and validation</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">TimeSeriesScientist <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al. (2025)</a></cite>; CLIMATEAGENT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite>; CastFlow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Pan et al. (2026)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Keep stage outputs explicit. Log retrieved evidence, tool calls, predictions, and validation results so later stages do not inherit hidden errors</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.2.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Can a reader inspect the artifact used by the next stage?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Numerical or domain reasoning errors</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Tasks that require temporal structure, metadata, domain conventions, or quantitative operations</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">TS-Agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib38" title="" class="ltx_ref">Liu et al. (2025)</a></cite>; TS-Reasoner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. (2024b)</a></cite>; CLIMATEAGENT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. (2025)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Let the LLM plan and explain, but move calculation and domain-specific parsing into tools, operators, or specialist agents</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.3.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Can the numerical claim be rerun outside the LLM?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Semantic drift in generated data</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Augmentation and synthesis, where plausible-looking outputs can break trend, periodicity, local shape, correlation, or domain constraints</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">DCATS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yeh et al. (2025)</a></cite>; MERIT <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib46" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. (2025)</a></cite>; BRIDGE <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2025)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.4.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Generate from target context and verify temporal properties before the synthetic data enters training or evaluation</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.4.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.4.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Do checks cover trend, seasonality, local shape, and correlation rather than textual plausibility alone?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Brittle LLM-as-judge validation</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Validation settings where a pretrained judge can approve an output without task evidence or executable checks</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.5.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">DCATS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib44" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yeh et al. (2025)</a></cite>; TS-Reasoner <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al. (2024b)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.5.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Treat LLM critique as one signal. Require task metrics, execution feedback, or downstream validation before accepting an output</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.5.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.5.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Would the output be rejected if another LLM approved it but the executable check failed?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.6" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Contamination during online updates</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Streaming anomaly detection, where transient anomalies can be absorbed as the new normal</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">CALM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib63" title="" class="ltx_ref">Devireddy and Huang (2025)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Separate alarm decisions from update decisions; gate which observations can enter memory or fine-tuning data</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.6.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.6.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Can short-lived anomalies be kept out of the update set?</span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A4.T2.2.1.7" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:69.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.1.1.1" class="ltx_p">Unsafe or infeasible actions in closed-loop control</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.2.1.1" class="ltx_p">Traffic and grid-control agents that issue executable actions under operational constraints</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.7.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.3.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:96.7pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.3.1.1" class="ltx_p">LLMLight <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib116" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lai et al. (2025)</a></cite>; Grid-Agent <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib78" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al. (2025d)</a></cite>; GridMind <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib62" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jin et al. (2025)</a></cite></span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.7.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.4.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:130.9pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.4.1.1" class="ltx_p">Check proposed actions with a simulator, solver, feasibility test, or safety validator before execution</span>
</span></td>
<td id="A4.T2.2.1.7.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb" style="padding:0.8pt 2.5pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.5.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:85.4pt;">
<span id="A4.T2.2.1.7.5.1.1" class="ltx_p">Does every action pass an environment or constraint check first?</span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Resources Summary</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ Decision and control metrics. ‣ Appendix F Evaluation Evidence and Metrics ‣ Appendix E Resources Summary ‣ Appendix D Failure Modes and Design Patterns ‣ Appendix C Typical Design Patterns ‣ B.4 Decision Support ‣ B.3 Anomaly Detection and Diagnosis ‣ B.2 Augmentation and Synthesis ‣ B.1 Forecasting and Reasoning ‣ Appendix B Representative Prompt Examples by Task Family ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> summarizes the resources discussed in Section <a href="#S5" title="5 Resources ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>, including benchmarks, datasets, environments, and toolkits. For each resource, we report its category, associated problem type, interactivity, temporal scale, number of series, and latest release when available.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Evaluation Evidence and Metrics</h2>

<div id="A6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A6.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Decision and control metrics. ‣ Appendix F Evaluation Evidence and Metrics ‣ Appendix E Resources Summary ‣ Appendix D Failure Modes and Design Patterns ‣ Appendix C Typical Design Patterns ‣ B.4 Decision Support ‣ B.3 Anomaly Detection and Diagnosis ‣ B.2 Augmentation and Synthesis ‣ B.1 Forecasting and Reasoning ‣ Appendix B Representative Prompt Examples by Task Family ‣ LLM Agents for Time-Series: A Survey" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> reports representative comparable quantitative evidence across forecasting, reasoning, anomaly detection, trading, and traffic-control tasks.
We only group results that share the same task, dataset, and metric, and we mark the surveyed agent methods in bold.
The table is intended as comparable evidence rather than a universal leaderboard: scores may still depend on horizon, split, point-adjustment rule, transaction-cost assumption, or simulator configuration.</p>
</div>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Error metrics.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Regression-style tasks usually report point-wise errors such as mean absolute error (MAE), mean squared error (MSE), and root mean squared error (RMSE):</p>
<table id="A6.Ex2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex2X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MAE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MAE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MAE}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|y_{i}-\hat{y}_{i}|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}|y_{i}-\hat{y}_{i}|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex2Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>MSE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{MSE}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_{i}-\hat{y}_{i})^{2}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^{n}(y_{i}-\hat{y}_{i})^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex2Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{RMSE}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>RMSE</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{RMSE}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex2Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\mathrm{MSE}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mi>MSE</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\mathrm{MSE}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the target and prediction for the <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th evaluated point, and <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of evaluated points. Lower values indicate better forecasts. Scale-free variants such as MAPE, sMAPE, or MASE are used when series with different magnitudes must be compared.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Classification and detection metrics.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Reasoning, event prediction, anomaly detection, and some augmentation studies are commonly evaluated with accuracy, precision, recall, and F1. Let TP, FP, and FN denote true positives, false positives, and false negatives:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex3" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A6.Ex3X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex3X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Precision}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Precision</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Precision}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex3X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FP}},\quad\mathrm{Recall}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FN}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>TP</mi><mrow><mi>TP</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FP</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>Recall</mi><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>TP</mi><mrow><mi>TP</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>FN</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FP}},\quad\mathrm{Recall}=\frac{\mathrm{TP}}{\mathrm{TP}+\mathrm{FN}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A6.Ex3Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex3Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{F1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F1</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{F1}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A6.Ex3Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=2\frac{\mathrm{Precision}\cdot\mathrm{Recall}}{\mathrm{Precision}+\mathrm{Recall}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Precision</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Recall</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>Precision</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>Recall</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=2\frac{\mathrm{Precision}\cdot\mathrm{Recall}}{\mathrm{Precision}+\mathrm{Recall}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Macro-F1 averages class-wise F1 and is useful under class imbalance; micro-F1 aggregates counts before computing F1. In anomaly detection, F1 can be point-wise, point-adjusted, or event-based, so comparisons require the same adjustment rule. Score-based detectors may additionally use AUROC or AUPR.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Generation and annotation metrics.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For augmentation and synthesis, evaluation is often indirect: generated samples are used to train or adapt a downstream model, and the downstream MAE, MSE, accuracy, or F1 is reported. Papers may also measure distributional fidelity with DTW, MMD, autocorrelation, spectral statistics, or nearest-neighbor analyses, and annotation quality with expert agreement or label accuracy.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Decision and control metrics.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Trading agents are evaluated by both return and risk. Cumulative return (CR) measures portfolio growth, while the Sharpe ratio (SR) measures risk-adjusted return:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{SR}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[R_{t}-R_{f}]}{\sigma(R_{t}-R_{f})}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>SR</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>f</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{SR}=\frac{\mathbb{E}[R_{t}-R_{f}]}{\sigma(R_{t}-R_{f})}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Maximum drawdown, volatility, and turnover further capture downside risk and trading cost sensitivity. Recent trading-agent benchmarks such as StockBench <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib76" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al. (2025)</a></cite> further stress multi-month sequential evaluation under daily market signals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Traffic-control agents are usually evaluated in closed-loop simulators. Average travel time (ATT) is the mean travel duration across vehicles:</p>
<table id="A6.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ATT}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(t_{i}^{\mathrm{exit}}-t_{i}^{\mathrm{entry}})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ATT</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>exit</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>entry</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ATT}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(t_{i}^{\mathrm{exit}}-t_{i}^{\mathrm{entry}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where lower ATT indicates more efficient traffic flow. Related metrics include waiting time, queue length, throughput, cumulative reward, and constraint violations.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<figure id="A6.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 3: </span>Summary of representative LLM-based agentic methods for time-series tasks. Each method is grouped by <span id="A6.T3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Problem Type</span> and further characterized by its publication year, venue or source, architecture, tools, and memory.</figcaption>
